#: ../../reference/programme.rst:4 6da3b4e3632847e09a3add58986c81fb
msgid "``programme.yaml``"
msgstr "``programme.yaml``"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:6 bf8e11cf648646e98f11ba9c52a1eda2
msgid ""
"One file per competition, and everything the app does comes out of it: "
"the track, the categories, the events each contests, the rounds of every "
"event with their distances, the running order of each day, the entry-file"
" layout and the communiqué register."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:11 f4d639d1d6a34435a1f3fce52605ddd8
msgid ""
"It is edited from the Programme page and written by an emitter of our own"
" (``core/programme.py``) with a **stable layout**: saving the same "
"programme twice gives the same bytes, and read → write → read returns the"
" same ``Competition``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:18 7f37ae9532374508afe25baddb1a819c
msgid ""
"A hand-written ``#`` comment is lost on the next write. Notes belong in "
"the ``note:`` fields — on a programme item, on a round — which round-trip"
" like everything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:24 97dee7e3269f4b128f68922a598c4560
msgid "Top level"
msgstr "Livello principale"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:47 1de9efa5bc7f47c0852630600abacb54
msgid ""
"``kind`` decides what a classification prints under the winner: a "
"*championship* names a champion, an *ordinary* meeting does not, and a "
"*trofeo_regioni* adds the team points classification to the statistics "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:53 41f7778d50fa473cbcecb3b51e68c4c9
msgid "``categories``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:61 6645ff76988d4486af53b45a3ac7ff31
msgid ""
"``accepts`` is what makes a category *open*: the licence codes admitted "
"into it, ``M*`` taking every master code. Riders keep their own licence "
"code beside the name. Standard codes come from "
"``regulations/categories.json``; anything else is declared here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:68 2722aaf4130d476185ab8bd49b942b26
msgid "``events``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:85 a804cf91a4fe4d9b972bf15438591337
msgid ""
"**What an event *is*** — code, abbreviation, format, riders per team, how"
" many start together — is the same at every meeting and lives in "
"``regulations/events.json``. The programme writes back only what it does "
"*differently*. The ``name`` always stays here, because it is what gets "
"printed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:90 572e475533de40d1b01ca0bed95e2758
msgid ""
"``fmt`` is one of ``group``, ``points``, ``tempo``, ``scratch``, "
"``madison``, ``elimination``, ``timed``, ``timed_team``, ``bracket``, "
"``derny``. See :ref:`formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:96 32f3aef369c64533893be0ab63226be0
msgid "``programme``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:98 777de282b65549ee8449a30639ad32a4
msgid ""
"One entry per **(category, event)** pair — one event, whatever number of "
"days it spans:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:118 a7f9ac6f5e974099ab0fdd3083af75d7
msgid ""
"The document kinds — ``partenti``, ``risultati``, ``classifica`` and the "
"rest — and the round keys are **stored values**, not labels: they are "
"what is written in this file and what race files are named after, so they"
" are reproduced here exactly as they must be typed. Translating one would"
" stop the app finding its own race. What the jury reads instead comes "
"from ``core.i18n``; see :ref:`i18n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:126 4ec690b245b14eb6a0be5cafbcfcd38d
msgid "Round fields"
msgstr "I campi di un round"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:132 06e3e669dcf24ad9b2d914d1e80135f9
msgid "Field"
msgstr "Campo"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:133 4974df453e384649ba6184c017c3ee5a
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "Significato"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:134 77c2b51374544a67a3093f05a6069fd7
msgid "``key``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:135 464dfddab53742ab9a90b408d31b2c10
msgid "The round's name. Written as it prints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:136 c0d5e80b0d1141da9e747830fd35ede6
msgid "``label``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:137 35fa13d76df14c7183d0bea665b79d7e
msgid "Display override, where the key is a technical one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:138 0473e071033f436a8da338bd28ba9fc3
msgid "``seq``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:139 b33f263b9d264707ab5bbc0d6eb493ab
msgid "Position in the day's running order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:140 d69d860d85d74b41aacaa6d3f3d8e8a5
msgid "``day``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:141 d5c987ac3c76442ca38da4329f0c7e86
msgid ""
"Which day this round is on. An event split across days is one entry with "
"rounds on different days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:143 45ad65b3a16d494aa227015fd5c2b684
msgid "``duration``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:144 297540ac3e3e42ffb6de400a3cc65fe4
msgid ""
"Minutes. **Start times are computed** from ``day_start`` plus the "
"durations before it, not typed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:146 218e6d86177044a49d0bf6346ca3014d
msgid "``distance`` / ``laps`` / ``sprints``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:147 b66a5af475ec4208bb2b52c968f9a0fd
msgid ""
"km, laps and number of sprints. An explicit value wins over the one "
"derived from ``regulations/distances.json`` and the track length: some "
"races do not follow the formula."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:150 16739d35663444bf9ae7d8f77884767a
msgid "``docs``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:151 c3cfd6ad59dc449ba1c332409f3cf0ea
msgid "Which sheets this round files. See :ref:`communiques`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:152 a15be850e44143688afbb09c05f6c9da
msgid "``heat_size``, ``qualify``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:153 624cdbca9a4946eea42a3d4aba494220
msgid "Sprint and keirin: riders per heat, how many advance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:154 65813b7edaf5493c9248e0cfb59bf829
msgid "``eliminate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:155 cd93536aac6c4e93a0387e91564e3512
msgid ""
"Madison and omnium qualifying heats: how many go out of each. UCI 3.2.157"
" puts the floor at 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:157 bc23cb1f8f27464da6dba9593af1c2e6
msgid "``kind``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:158 de5fa795c0a24bb6aac5def2d79651b3
msgid ""
"``setup`` for a round that is composed rather than ridden; ``pause`` for "
"a break in the running order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:160 1b0f42ec6629462c94252a431dd06713
msgid "``note`` / ``sheet_note`` / ``results_note``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:161 64f38e7c668d40c896015a50ce3c0470
msgid ""
"A service note (not printed), and the lines the start order and the "
"results sheet open on (printed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:164 94d938140b3f45f09c308d143b3b8a20
msgid ""
"A **pause** is a round with ``kind: pause`` — no category, no event, no "
"communiqués. It exists because an hour the programme does not count is an"
" hour every time below it is wrong about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:170 bb5156e148d445eea7d4014170b5856c
msgid "``communiques``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:172 39bb839061c04928bac5d12f90c2f7a7
msgid "The register. One entry per numbered sheet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:185 a2dd444839bc402da705a55bd29568df
msgid ""
"``with:`` is how one number carries more than one sheet — a bare document"
" kind inherits the entry's own category, event and round; a mapping "
"overrides what it names. An empty ``round: \"\"`` means the sheet belongs"
" to the *event*, not to any round of it, which is what a classification "
"is. ``pinned: true`` freezes a number against recalculation. See "
":ref:`communiques`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:193 f146fadc8492466ba9efc63a69499852
msgid "``checks``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:195 de27642a80dd4eb2b74bb85ea6cf501c
msgid "One row per sentence of the regulation's article on entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:204 3aa1e7d79f3c48229f64f01320b2572a
msgid ""
"``cat`` and ``event`` take a code or ``*``; ``unit`` is ``riders``, "
"``teams``, ``pairs`` or ``events``; ``per`` is ``region``, ``club``, "
"``club_in_region``, ``cat`` or ``rider`` (the last only with ``unit: "
"events``); ``max: 0`` switches the row off; ``level`` is ``error``, "
"``warn`` or ``off``; ``count_reserves`` says whether reserve entries "
"count; ``note`` is the article, printed at the foot of every finding the "
"rule raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:211 d8db5f014f934285a0b5bcbc8262a29d
msgid ""
"**Nothing here blocks.** A rule set to ``error`` is red at the licence "
"desk and counts in the summary; the meeting saves, prints and runs "
"regardless. A derogation is the jury's to grant, not the file's to "
"refuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:217 e12d05df24e04d79bf91ce4cdf17a2ad
msgid "``entries``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:219 ec024b1e478b41efa05a5c28d56cefd3
msgid "How the entry file is read and what a team is at this meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:235 d3c922f5d0c549fea74e3b3b807907d4
msgid ""
"Column headings are matched **by name, never by position**, so a shifted "
"column does not silently import garbage and a differently-worded export "
"is a config change rather than a code change. What a competition states "
"here wins over the format's own table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:242 445726f977f94bbb8035af23b054bcb0
msgid ""
"The ``check_in`` keys are the literal column headings of the federation's"
" workbook, which is why ``NP`` appears there: it is a heading in a file, "
"not a result code. The code for a rider who will not start is ``NS`` — "
"see the :ref:`glossary`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:247 e38498d12d224fcca9cd5bd7c7b54d0a
msgid ""
"``team_merge`` is the derogation where two regions field one team: it "
"changes how the teams of those events are composed and the name they race"
" under, and nothing else — every rider stays in their own region for "
"individual events, quotas and the per-team recap. See :ref:`entries`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:254 bfb0bf13f1884b6e9755a094f68faee7
msgid "``branding`` and ``merge``"
msgstr "``branding`` e ``merge``"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:256 fb4e55a241754d9d832fe7fd9cd1ec90
msgid ""
"``branding`` is how a sheet looks: header and footer images and their "
"fit, the header-line and footer-line slots, the signature, the name "
"style, the decision colours, the fonts and the text colours. All of it is"
" edited from the settings page; see :ref:`printing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:261 f88a63ccf0d7495aaa9224a504fcb2f6
msgid ""
"``merge`` names which of the five communiqué merge rules are in force for"
" this competition, **by exception only**: what is not named here follows "
"``regulations/communiques.json``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:272 a30d422a47fc435e87f278507ca28854
msgid "Validation"
msgstr "Validazione"

#: ../../reference/programme.rst:274 e524738131a049aba84bc84d61971be3
msgid ""
"``core.programme.validate`` runs before every save. The Programme page's "
"save control stays disabled while any finding is at ``error`` level: a "
"duplicate communiqué number, a communiqué already issued that now points "
"at a different sheet, a round on no day. Everything else is a warning and"
" saves."
msgstr ""

